(20,0,'ArrayQ01','<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Write a function to enter values type real into an array size n. A prototype of that array is<br>void ArrInput(float,int)</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Write a function to display the value of elements of an integer array on the screen. A prototype of that array is</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">void ArrShow(float,int)</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Note: Don\'t have a space at the end of the row.</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Input:<br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">1</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">2<br>3<br>4<br>5<br>Output:<br>1 2 3 4 5<br><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\"><br></p>',1,'',1,1.0000000,0.0000000,'coderunner',1,'unknownhost+260921032619+MovkVd',1789961179,1789961179,2,2),
(21,0,'ArrayQ02','<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Define ArrInitial function to initial an array by assigning numbers from 1 to n into an array size of n.</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Define ArrShowVer function to show elements of an array in the vertical direction.</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Input: 1 2</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Output:</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">1</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">2<br></p>',1,'',1,1.0000000,0.0000000,'coderunner',1,'unknownhost+260921032619+pzp3kn',1789961179,1789961179,2,2),
(22,0,'ArrayQ03','<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Define ArrInitial function to copy the value of each element real from a source array into a destination array.</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\"><br></p>',1,'',1,1.0000000,0.0000000,'coderunner',1,'unknownhost+260921032619+0fycVC',1789961179,1789961179,2,2),
(23,0,'ArrayQ04','<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Define ArrPrimes to print out all primes in an array, size of n, such that there are 10 numbers in a row.</p>',1,'',1,1.0000000,0.0000000,'coderunner',1,'unknownhost+260921032619+WNK95z',1789961179,1789961179,2,2),
(24,0,'ArrayQ05','<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Define ArrSumPerfects to the sum of all perfect square numbers in an array, size n, and return the result.</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">4 is perfect square numbers = 2*2</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Input:&nbsp;</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Array =&nbsp; {2 3 4 5 9}</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Output: 13<br></p>',1,'',1,1.0000000,0.0000000,'coderunner',1,'unknownhost+260921032619+Mus0GQ',1789961179,1789961179,2,2),
(25,0,'ArrayQ06','<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Define a function named ArrCountSymmetric to count all symmetric numbers in an array, size n, and return the result.</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Input:</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Array = {1,11,12}</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Output: 2<br></p>',1,'',1,1.0000000,0.0000000,'coderunner',1,'unknownhost+260921032619+vUydUG',1789961179,1789961179,2,2),
(26,0,'ArrayQ07','<p>Define a function named ArrCount_SumDigitsDivisibleBy3 to count all numbers that sum of digits divided by 3 in an array, size n, and return the result.</p><p>Input:</p><p>Array = {11, 3, 12}</p><p>Output: 2<br></p>',1,'',1,1.0000000,0.0000000,'coderunner',1,'unknownhost+260921032619+4yj5A3',1789961179,1789961179,2,2),
(27,0,'ArrayQ08','<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Define a function named ArrMax to return the maximum value of a double array, size n.</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Input:</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Array = {1,3,8,9}</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Output: 9<br></p>',1,'',1,1.0000000,0.0000000,'coderunner',1,'unknownhost+260921032619+pszwkS',1789961179,1789961179,2,2),
(28,0,'ArrayQ09','<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Given an integer array consisting of n elements and K key value. Define ArrFindK function to determine either K in the array. The function returns first index of the array, if it is found, otherwise returns -1</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Input:</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Array = {1,3,6,8,2}, K = 6</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Output: 2<br></p>',1,'',1,1.0000000,0.0000000,'coderunner',1,'unknownhost+260921032619+PDHo6p',1789961179,1789961179,2,2),
(29,0,'ArrayQ10','<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Given an integer array consisting of n elements. Define ArrEvenMax function to determine the even element has the largest value. If there are no elements in the array, the result will be -8080.</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Input:</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Array = {2,3,5,6,9}</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Output: 6<br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\"><br></p>',1,'',1,1.0000000,0.0000000,'coderunner',1,'unknownhost+260921032619+n9QdFd',1789961179,1789961179,2,2),
(30,0,'ArrayQ11','<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Given a numeric array consisting of n elements. Define ArrMostOccurence function to determine the element with the most occurrences in the array. <br>If there are multiple elements with the same number of occurrences, choose which element appears first in the array. <br>Outputs the element and its number of occurrences.</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Input:</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Array {10, 11, 12, 13, 14}</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Output: 10 1<br></p>',1,'',1,1.0000000,0.0000000,'coderunner',1,'unknownhost+260921032619+NTkQHh',1789961179,1789961179,2,2),
(31,0,'ArrayQ12','<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Determines the kth odd element in the array and returns its value (returns \"-1\" if it doesn\'t exist).<br>Prototype of the function is: int FindKthOddArray(int A[], int size, int k)</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Input: k = 2<br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Array {9, 2, 6, 3, 0, 5}</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Output:</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">3<br></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\"><br></p>',1,'',1,1.0000000,0.0000000,'coderunner',1,'unknownhost+260921032619+sLxFyS',1789961179,1789961179,2,2),
(32,0,'ArrayQ13','<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Define ArrDistanceEuclid to calculate the Euclidean distance of 2 vectors presented by 2 two arrays, size n.</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\"><br></p>',1,'',1,1.0000000,0.0000000,'coderunner',1,'unknownhost+260921032619+pyEKaZ',1789961179,1789961179,2,2),
(33,0,'ArrayQ14','<p>Define ArrMerge function to input two one-dimensional arrays in order and merge those into a third array that must be ordered too. And display the result of the third array that was ordered. The size of each array is 500.<br></p><p>Input:</p><p>Array1 {1,2,3,4}</p><p>Array2 {3,5,6}</p><p>Output</p><p>Array3 {1,2,3,3,4,5}<br></p>',1,'',1,1.0000000,0.0000000,'coderunner',1,'unknownhost+260921032619+MBERUr',1789961179,1789961179,2,2),
(34,0,'ArrayQ15','<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Define ArrFrequency function to calculate the number of occurrences of each element in the array, size 10000, and output as the following format. And the space between each column is a TAB</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Input:</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Array {2,3,2,4}</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Output:</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Value&nbsp;&nbsp; Frequency<br>2&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 2<br>3&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 1<br>4&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 1<br></p>',1,'',1,1.0000000,0.0000000,'coderunner',1,'unknownhost+260921032619+79T6ey',1789961179,1789961179,2,2),
