(39,0,'ControlQ05','<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Write a program input a year if that year is a leap year then output \"yes\" else \"no\"<br>Know that A leap year has 366 days (the extra day is the 29th of February). <br><br>How to know if it is a Leap Year: <br>- Leap Years are any year that can be exactly divided by 4 (such as 2016, 2020, 2024, etc)<br>- except if it can be exactly divided by 100, then it isn\'t (such as 2100, 2200, etc)<br>- except if it can be exactly divided by 400, then it is (such as 2000, 2400)</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Input&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Output<br>2011&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; NOT a Leap Year<br>1900&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; NOT a Leap Year<br>2000&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Leap Year<br>2012&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Leap Year<br><br></p>',1,'',1,1.0000000,0.0000000,'coderunner',1,'unknownhost+260921032619+yTTBp9',1789961179,1789961179,2,2),
(40,0,'ControlQ06','<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Write a program input month, year then calculate day numbers in that month. Know that A leap year has 366 days <br>(the extra day is the 29th of February). <br><br>How to know if it is a Leap Year: <br>- Leap Years are any year that can be exactly divided by 4 (such as 2016, 2020, 2024, etc)<br>- except if it can be exactly divided by 100, then it isn\'t (such as 2100, 2200, etc)<br>- except if it can be exactly divided by 400, then it is (such as 2000, 2400)<br><br></p>',1,'',1,1.0000000,0.0000000,'coderunner',1,'unknownhost+260921032619+Qa6soX',1789961179,1789961179,2,2),
