(46,0,'ControlQ11','<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">A bank needs a program that charges a customer\'s bank account. &nbsp;<br>The customer\'s bank ID number consists of four digits. <br>Customers can have a savings account (S) or payment account (C). <br>The bank charges customers $5.00 per month for one savings account and $7.50 for a payment account. <br>If the customer has more than four withdrawals in a month, they have to pay an extra $2.50 for each additional withdrawal. <br>Customer IDs and the bank charges for the next month will be issued to the customer.<br><br>Write a program to calculate bank charge and show information account of the customer when the employee enter the account type and number of withdrawals.<br>Note: If input of account type and withdrawals are wrong then show \"Incorrect\" and $0.00 for bank charge on the screen.<br>Using TAB for spaces between columns<br><br>Input: S 3<br>Output:<br>AccountType&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Withdrawals&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; BankCharge<br>S&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 3&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; $5.00<br><br>a 4<br>AccountType&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Withdrawals&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; BankCharge<br>Incorrect&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 4&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; $0.00<br>C -2<br>AccountType&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Withdrawals&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; BankCharge<br>C&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Incorrect&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; $0.00<br><br></p>',1,'',1,1.0000000,0.0000000,'coderunner',1,'unknownhost+260921032619+3jyxIS',1789961179,1789961179,2,2),
(47,0,'ControlQ12','Write a program to input a character from the keyboard, then output the Ascii code and its capital letter if the character is a vowel. <br>Otherwise, output the Ascii code and the character is not a vowel. Know the vowels {\'a\', \'e\', \'i\', \'o\', \'u\', \'y\'}<br><br><br>Input1:<br>letter = a<br>Output1:<br>65: A<br><br>Input2:<br>letter = A<br>Output2:<br>65: A<br><br>Input3:<br>letter = f<br>Output3:<br>102: f is not a vowel<br><br>Input4:<br>letter = F<br>Output4:<br>102: F is not a vowel<br><br><br><br><br>',1,'',1,1.0000000,0.0000000,'coderunner',1,'unknownhost+260921032619+9eQxsA',1789961179,1789961179,2,2),
(48,0,'Function1','<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\">The formula for calculating a person\'s BMI when knowing their weight (kg) and height (m) is as follows:<br>And BMI according to the recommendations of the World Health Organization (WHO) (except for pregnant people):<br><br>BMI less than 18.5 status is \"underweight\"<br>BMI between 18.5 and 22.99 status is “normal”<br>BMI between 23 and 24.99 status as “overweight”<br>BMI &gt; 25 status is “obese”<br><br>Implement BMI function that enter weight and height of a person then calulate and return person\'s BMI<br>Implement Obesefunction that enter BMI of a person and display person\'s state <br><br><br></p>',1,'',1,1.0000000,0.0000000,'coderunner',1,'unknownhost+260921032619+vVPFAC',1789961179,1789961179,2,2),
